  "notes": "Logo is the site's header logo (SVG, 2019/10/logo.svg). A reverse version is at https://www.sunreef.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/logo_rev-1.svg (probably for dark backgrounds). No heroImage given in this file: the facts file uses 2022/09/2017-1-scaled.jpg (a large scaled photo on the whale watching page), which was not viewed, so a person should check it is a plain wide photo. Left out: Website-Home-banner.png (the home page hero, a banner), the Eco Certified Ecotourism badge and social icons, Canva-style graphics (Untitled-design-1.png, sUNSHINE-cOASTLINE2.png, block-2.png), the cultural cruises painting (Beeyali_Whale_Painting_Hero), the home page tiles, and the Instagram and Facebook feeds. Credited photos left out: the 16-photo slider on the ex-HMAS Brisbane page sits directly above 'Photo credits: Colin Baker' and 'Matt Shepherd Nudibranchs of the Sunshine Coast', so those files were not used anywhere (including files of the same name on other pages: 2019/08/9.jpg, 2019/08/10.jpg, 2019/08/4-1.jpg, 2019/10/22.jpg, 2019/10/23-1.jpg). The Brisbane-firing-TARTAR-Missile.jpg is a historical navy image. Turtle-with-sun-behind-Matt-Shepherd.jpg is named for another photographer. The Nudibranch Double Dive page credits its photos to Gary Cobb (nudibranch.com.au), so that trip has no photos. Other pages carry no credit lines, but the numbered underwater files (2019/08 to 2019/11) may come from the same photographers, so a person should confirm ownership. Photos were chosen from the file names and pages only (none were downloaded or viewed); header-*.jpg files are page header photos and may include darkened or cropped backgrounds. A few were checked to load (logo, 2017-1-scaled.jpg, header-1-3.jpg, 12-2.jpg, use2.jpg, 1.png). Three files in the Whale One sets have Facebook-style numeric names (276156008_..., 275929354_..., 275943965_...); they are on Sunreef's own pages. 2023/11/1.png on the Coral Conservation Survey Dive page is a PNG that was not checked for text. Videos are the four YouTube embeds on the home page and the ex-HMAS Brisbane page; titles come from the embed titles and were shortened. The swim with whales page also embeds one titled as a 2017 season update with P&O Cruises in the title; it was left out as it may belong to another business. No YouTube channel link was found on the pages read, and YouTube was not opened. Many trip pages have only one to three photos. All pages answered normally; no captcha or bot check was met."
